{"candidate_id": "cand-ap-altnews-0021", "factchecker": "altnews.in", "factcheck_article": "https://www.altnews.in/video-of-dhaka-eviction-drive-falsely-claimed-as-bjp-bulldozer-action-against-bangladeshis-in-bengal/", "social_url": "https://www.facebook.com/reel/1005432212022241", "media_url": "https://www.facebook.com/reel/1005432212022241", "platform": "facebook", "media_type": "photo", "ground_truth_claim": null, "ground_truth_label": null, "claim_type": "provenance", "language": "en", "eligibility_status": "REJECTED", "rejection_reason": "Judged NOT the misinformation source (conf=1.00): [\"The Facebook post's caption translates to 'Even if you cry for mercy, they can't protect themselves'\", \"This claim is false because the video shows a demolition of structures without issuing prior eviction notices.\", \"According to Ekattor TV news report, police tried to demolish structures in Bauniabandh area of Mirpur, Dhaka on May 20. This information corroborates with the address seen on the hoarding of 'Khan Bastro Bitan'.\"]", "judge_confidence": null, "history": [{"status": "DISCOVERED", "at": "2026-09-07T13:06:57.979441+00:00", "note": "created"}, {"status": "SOCIAL_REFERENCE_FOUND", "at": "2026-09-07T13:06:57.980470+00:00", "note": "facebook ref via mass_source_allplatform.py"}, {"status": "MEDIA_RETRIEVABLE", "at": "2026-09-07T13:07:00.780588+00:00", "note": "uploader=61573651922468 caption=True video=False"}, {"status": "REJECTED", "at": "2026-09-07T13:07:36.988901+00:00", "note": "llama3.2: [\"The Facebook post's caption translates to 'Even if you cry for mercy, they can't protect themselves'\", \"This claim is false because the video shows a demolition of structures without issuing prior eviction notices.\", \"According to Ekattor TV news report, police tried to demolish structures in Bauniabandh area of Mirpur, Dhaka on May 20. This information corroborates with the address seen on the hoarding of 'Khan Bastro Bitan'.\"]"}]}
{"candidate_id": "cand-ap-altnews-0022", "factchecker": "altnews.in", "factcheck_article": "https://www.altnews.in/video-of-dhaka-eviction-drive-falsely-claimed-as-bjp-bulldozer-action-against-bangladeshis-in-bengal/", "social_url": "https://www.facebook.com/reel/1579873576807859", "media_url": "https://www.facebook.com/reel/1579873576807859", "platform": "facebook", "media_type": "photo", "ground_truth_claim": null, "ground_truth_label": null, "claim_type": "provenance", "language": "en", "eligibility_status": "REJECTED", "rejection_reason": "Judged NOT the misinformation source (conf=1.00): ...the caption of the video says: \u201cBangladeshi slums in West Bengal are witnessing Bulldozer action.\u2022 All these slums were built on the encroached lands of the forest department and other government departments...\\n\nThe same video was shared by several other social media users, between May 21 and May 22, which helped it to go viral. Fact Check While playing the video, at 35-36 second mark, at the bottom right corner of the video, one can see a boom used by the news media...\\n\nAlso at the 28 second mark, the video shows the hoarding of a shop called \u2019Khan Bastro Bitan\u2032. The hoarding contains a name- Abdul Kuddus Khan, and a contact number....\n\nAlong with that, the hoarding of \u2018Khan Bastro Bitan\u2019 mentions Dhaka, Mirpur-1216, which is the postal code for the Mirpur suburb of Dhaka...\\n\nAs we became sure that this video is from Bangladesh, we did a keyword search on Google, using the keywords-\u201cHome demolished eviction drive Bangladesh family in tears\u2032....\nThe caption of the video says: Entire family breaks down in tears as their house is demolished. \u2018Sobar Kantha\u2019 posted the now viral video on their Facebook page on May 20, 2026...\\n\n\u2018Sobar Kantha\u2019 posted a series of short videos covering the May 20 incident....\nThe unconsolable man seen in the viral video is also seen in another video posted on that day, further proving that the now viral video is indeed from Bangladesh...", "judge_confidence": null, "history": [{"status": "DISCOVERED", "at": "2026-09-07T13:06:57.984779+00:00", "note": "created"}, {"status": "SOCIAL_REFERENCE_FOUND", "at": "2026-09-07T13:06:57.986019+00:00", "note": "facebook ref via mass_source_allplatform.py"}, {"status": "MEDIA_RETRIEVABLE", "at": "2026-09-07T13:07:00.790315+00:00", "note": "uploader=61573651922468 caption=True video=False"}, {"status": "REJECTED", "at": "2026-09-07T13:07:29.122869+00:00", "note": "llama3.2: ...the caption of the video says: \u201cBangladeshi slums in West Bengal are witnessing Bulldozer action.\u2022 All these slums were built on the encroached lands of the forest department and other government departments...\\n\nThe same video was shared by several other social media users, between May 21 and May 22, which helped it to go viral. Fact Check While playing the video, at 35-36 second mark, at the bottom right corner of the video, one can see a boom used by the news media...\\n\nAlso at the 28 second mark, the video shows the hoarding of a shop called \u2019Khan Bastro Bitan\u2032. The hoarding contains a name- Abdul Kuddus Khan, and a contact number....\n\nAlong with that, the hoarding of \u2018Khan Bastro Bitan\u2019 mentions Dhaka, Mirpur-1216, which is the postal code for the Mirpur suburb of Dhaka...\\n\nAs we became sure that this video is from Bangladesh, we did a keyword search on Google, using the keywords-\u201cHome demolished eviction drive Bangladesh family in tears\u2032....\nThe caption of the video says: Entire family breaks down in tears as their house is demolished. \u2018Sobar Kantha\u2019 posted the now viral video on their Facebook page on May 20, 2026...\\n\n\u2018Sobar Kantha\u2019 posted a series of short videos covering the May 20 incident....\nThe unconsolable man seen in the viral video is also seen in another video posted on that day, further proving that the now viral video is indeed from Bangladesh..."}]}
